    ('P-S056', 'Inside a warm Alpine cabin, the howl of a snowstorm is softened by thick walls while fine snow brushes the window. The contrast between the enclosed room and the weather beyond creates a sheltered nighttime atmosphere for settling down to rest. Without piercing peaks or window bangs interrupting the setting, the sound holds a measured shape that feels present without becoming intrusive or overly active around you. During quiet bedtime listening, Blizzard outside an Alpine Cabin offers a predictable sense of place that can remain softly present while the rest of the day begins to recede.'),
    ('P-S059', 'Imagine a sheltered place beneath the Amazon canopy at night, where distant tree frogs call through a rich layer of tropical insects. Faint rain remains beyond the leaves, giving the wildlife a soft background as you settle into this immersive evening scene. By leaving out close screeches or monkeys, the scene gives its quieter details room to breathe and remains uncluttered rather than busy or unpredictable. Amazon Jungle at Night suits quiet bedtime listening by keeping the listening experience calm and consistent, with enough detail to feel immersive without becoming demanding.'),
    ('P-F024', 'A light breeze moves through an aspen grove in the foothills of New Mexico, setting layers of leaves fluttering at different distances. Their fine, papery rustle gives this early-autumn afternoon a gentle sense of motion, suited to working quietly with a little natural detail nearby. The scene leaves out human activity or birds, allowing the central sounds to develop at an even pace without an abrupt distraction taking over the listening space. Used for light admin and preference-led focus, Rustling Aspen Leaves creates a consistent surrounding atmosphere that can accompany concentration without competing with it.'),
