    ('P-S030', 'Heard from a sheltered spot well back from the falls, a waterfall becomes a soft, continuous rush across the night. The distance blends its movement into a low, even wash, creating a spacious natural background for winding down. The night setting is heard from a sheltered listening point, keeping the experience connected as its steady pattern continues. The foreground remains free of roaring peaks or birds, preserving the scene''s calm balance and letting its softer textures carry the atmosphere from moment to moment. Distant Waterfall suits quiet bedtime listening by keeping the listening experience calm and consistent, with enough detail to feel immersive without becoming demanding.'),
    ('P-F055', 'Dusk settles beneath a Borneo rainforest canopy as tropical insects and distant tree frogs form a layered chorus. Faint rain overhead and softened leaf drips sit behind the wildlife, bringing a rich, gently changing natural setting to an evening of light work. Without close piercing calls or dramatic animal cries interrupting the setting, the sound holds a measured shape that feels present without becoming intrusive or overly active around you. Used for reading and sustained desk work, Rainforest Canopy in Borneo creates a consistent surrounding atmosphere that can accompany concentration without competing with it.'),
    ('P-S009', 'A slowly turning ceiling fan fills a quiet bedroom with soft, repeating airflow and a warm motor hum. Its gentle flutter gives the night a familiar rhythm, offering a simple background while you settle into bed. The night setting is heard from a sheltered indoor viewpoint, keeping the experience connected as its steady pattern continues. By leaving out rattles or switch clicks, the scene gives its quieter details room to breathe and remains uncluttered rather than busy or unpredictable. For quiet bedtime listening, the restrained atmosphere of Ceiling Fan can sit quietly in the room, giving attention a gentle place to settle as the day winds down.'),
    ('P-F049', 'Light morning rain falls across leaves and paving just beyond a sheltered garden doorway. Crisp droplets mingle with gentle runoff in an open, airy space, creating a fresh background for starting work or easing into a morning of reading. The scene leaves out thunder or isolated loud splashes, allowing the central sounds to develop at an even pace without an abrupt distraction taking over the listening space. During reading and sustained desk work, the gently absorbing world of Gentle Morning Rain can fill the room without asking you to follow every small shift.'),
    ('P-F042', 'At a reading desk in a quiet university library, distant pages turn and light footsteps pass between the shelves. A subdued ventilation hum holds the room together, creating a gently occupied daytime setting for spending time with your own reading or study. You will not hear intelligible speech or sung vocals; the natural rhythm remains clear, spacious, and easy to keep in the background for longer stretches. Quiet University Library is especially suited to desk work with shared-space ambience, bringing a steady sense of place while your main attention stays with whatever you are doing.'),
    ('P-F050', 'A fast-moving Alpine stream tumbles over closely spaced stones, filling the scene with a dense, continuous rush. Small eddies overlap beneath the brighter water sounds, offering an energetic natural background for a focused daytime session. The daytime setting is heard from a sheltered listening point, keeping the experience connected as its natural variation pattern continues. The listening space stays clear of isolated loud splashes or birds, so each subtle change can arrive gently and pass without demanding a response or close attention. Used for reading and sustained desk work, Rushing Alpine Stream creates a consistent surrounding atmosphere that can accompany concentration without competing with it.'),
    ('P-F001', 'Settle into an enclosed carriage on a journey through Tohoku, Japan, where the smooth hiss of the wheels blends with a gentle cabin hum. The even flow of ventilation keeps the afternoon atmosphere steady, offering a quiet travelling backdrop for reading or working through a task. The foreground remains free of human activity or station stops, preserving the scene''s calm balance and letting its softer textures carry the atmosphere from moment to moment. For reading and sustained desk work, Bullet Train through Japan offers enough texture to hold the background while leaving your attention free to remain with the task in front of you.'),
    ('P-R004', 'A spring morning in a wetland inspired by the Danube Delta carries reed-bird chatter across still water. Light water movements sit beneath the distant calls, creating a gently animated marshland scene for stepping away from a busy day and listening at leisure. Without human activity or boat engines interrupting the setting, the sound holds a measured shape that feels present without becoming intrusive or overly active around you. During unwinding and place immersion, the atmosphere of Springtime Marsh gives you somewhere unhurried to place your attention while the surrounding moment grows quieter.'),
    ('P-F003', 'Imagine a morning journey along the Danube through Austria''s Wachau region, heard from behind the glass of an electric riverboat cabin. A fine motor whirr meets the steady hiss of water at the bow, forming a smooth background for a focused stretch of desk work. By leaving out human activity or docking, the scene gives its quieter details room to breathe and remains uncluttered rather than busy or unpredictable. Riverboat on the Danube is especially suited to reading and sustained desk work, bringing a steady sense of place while your main attention stays with whatever you are doing.'),
    ('P-S057', 'Crickets fill a sheltered pine clearing after dark, with occasional owl hoots sounding from farther away. Soft movement passes through the canopy above, bringing a gently living woodland atmosphere to your evening wind-down. The night setting is heard from a sheltered listening point, keeping the experience connected as its gentle natural variation pattern continues. The scene leaves out close owl cries or branch snaps, allowing the central sounds to develop at an even pace without an abrupt distraction taking over the listening space. Chosen for quiet bedtime listening, Nighttime Forest can accompany the transition into rest with an atmosphere that stays composed and easy to leave in the background.'),
    ('P-F018', 'Along a low bank in Finland''s Kainuu forests, a wide river carries a deep, even rush through the summer afternoon. Subtle bubbles from a shoreline eddy add detail beneath the current, offering a full, continuous water background for time spent concentrating. You will not hear human activity or birds; the natural rhythm remains clear, spacious, and easy to keep in the background for longer stretches. For reading and sustained desk work, Deep Forest River offers enough texture to hold the background while leaving your attention free to remain with the task in front of you.')
  )
  SELECT
    count(*),
    count(DISTINCT catalogue_ref),
    count(*) FILTER (WHERE length(trim(detail_description)) = 0),
    ARRAY(
      SELECT d.catalogue_ref
      FROM descriptions AS d
      GROUP BY d.catalogue_ref
      HAVING count(*) > 1
      ORDER BY d.catalogue_ref
    ),
    ARRAY(
      SELECT d.catalogue_ref
      FROM descriptions AS d
      WHERE cardinality(string_to_array(trim(d.detail_description), ' ')) NOT BETWEEN 90 AND 140
      ORDER BY d.catalogue_ref
    ),
    ARRAY(
      SELECT d.catalogue_ref
      FROM descriptions AS d
      LEFT JOIN public.soundscapes AS s ON s.catalogue_ref = d.catalogue_ref
      WHERE s.catalogue_ref IS NULL
      ORDER BY d.catalogue_ref
    ),
    ARRAY(
      SELECT s.catalogue_ref
      FROM public.soundscapes AS s
      JOIN descriptions AS d ON d.catalogue_ref = s.catalogue_ref
      GROUP BY s.catalogue_ref
      HAVING count(*) > 1
      ORDER BY s.catalogue_ref
    )
  INTO
    supplied_count,
    distinct_count,
    blank_count,
    duplicate_supplied_refs,
    invalid_length_refs,
    missing_refs,
    duplicate_database_refs
  FROM descriptions;

  IF supplied_count <> 93 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Expected 93 supplied descriptions, found %. No changes committed.', supplied_count;
  END IF;
  IF distinct_count <> 93 OR cardinality(duplicate_supplied_refs) > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Duplicate supplied catalogue references: %. No changes committed.', array_to_string(duplicate_supplied_refs, ', ');
  END IF;
  IF blank_count > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Found % blank detail descriptions. No changes committed.', blank_count;
  END IF;
  IF cardinality(invalid_length_refs) > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Descriptions outside 90-140 words: %. No changes committed.', array_to_string(invalid_length_refs, ', ');
  END IF;
  IF cardinality(missing_refs) > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Missing catalogue references: %. No changes committed.', array_to_string(missing_refs, ', ');
  END IF;
  IF cardinality(duplicate_database_refs) > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Duplicate catalogue references in public.soundscapes: %. No changes committed.', array_to_string(duplicate_database_refs, ', ');
  END IF;
END
$validate$;

